  "description": {
    "text": "The Rayquaza Mega Battle was Japan's spring championship of 2015: tournaments in Nagoya on 5 May, at Makuhari Messe on 9 and 10 May, Sapporo Factory on 23 and 24 May and Intex Osaka on 31 May, and a Japan Championship at Pokémon Center Osaka on 27 and 28 June whose top finishers were invited to the World Championships in Boston that August. Players qualified through the Rayquaza Gym Battle in March and the Rayquaza Pokémon Center Battle in March and April, or through the Last Challenge qualifier at each venue. A first-round win in the qualifier earned a Mega Turbo, the top three of each league won Victory Ring in gold, silver or bronze stamped with the event's logo, and Play Points bought prizes such as a Gym Badge for three points or M Swampert-EX for nine.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokémon Card Game official site: Rayquaza Mega Battle",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon-card.com/event/card-event/rmb/"
      },
